<abstract type="Summary">The new C₁₉-diterpenoid alkaloid 19-oxo-14-acetylbrowniine (1) and the alkaloid shawurensine for the first time were isolated from the plant Delphinium oreophilum collected in Jizzakh Region, Uzbekistan. The structure of the new alkaloid was elucidated using IR, 1D, and 2D NMR spectroscopy and high-resolution mass spectrometry. Compound 1 demonstrated high (78.6%) antioxidant activity for neutralization of DPPH (2,2-diphenyl-1-picrylhydrazyl) radicals vs. ascorbic acid as a positive control.</abstract>
